  "source_claim": {
    "summary": [
      "If the discontinuous analytic quotient Y=X/G is compact, equivalence classes with fixed endpoints of equivariant holomorphic vector-bundle extensions of E by F form a finite-dimensional complex vector space.",
      "More generally, if A and B are coherent analytic sheaves with operators, Ext^i_{O,G}(X;A,B) is finite-dimensional for every i."
    ],
    "scope_boundary": [
      "compactness is imposed on Y, not X",
      "G may be infinite and the action need not be free; discontinuity supplies finite stabilizers",
      "the statement does not make q globally finite or proper",
      "finite dimensionality is not finiteness of the set of extension classes",
      "the following abstract algebraic analogue and its characteristic hypotheses are separate",
      "no Ext vanishing, finite projective dimension, moduli representability, algebraization, or GAGA claim is made"
    ],
    "source_repair_required": false,
    "transcription_or_translation_repair_required": false,
    "existing_admitted_repair": "TOH-P219-COR-001 already changes diplomatic `Y est compacte` to corrected `Y est compact`; no new repair is appended."
  },
